3144 kíṁcid 'anything' RV. [n. sg. of káścid: ká -²] Pa. kiñci ; Aś. kiṁci , NiDoc. kiṁci , na iṁci 'nothing';
Pk. kiṁci 'anything, a little'; Gy. pers. hič 'nothing', gr. ič , hič 'something, nothing', wel. čī 'anything' J. Bloch
BSL 129, 46., Bshk. kičə ; Si. kis 'anything, whatever,
all'; — with - cch - from m. káścid : L. kijh , kujh 'some';
WPah. bhal. kich 'some, a little'; A. kisu 'a little, a few';
B. Mth. kichu 'something, anything', OH. kachū , H. kuch . Addenda: kíṁcid: WPah.kṭg. kíċċh , kiċ 'something, anything'
( kúċċh , kuċ ← H.).
